        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "The reason to care is the trio language, not a scarcity gimmick. Hara's music lives in the space between piano, electronics, chamber texture and film-score silence; Suhara and Tai are already embedded in that current sound world rather than appearing as decorative strings. In a club-sized room, the interesting question is how that carefully layered language turns back into live three-way interaction, especially after the scale and visibility of Kokuho.",
